00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.080
<b>I'll be back.</b>

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.040
<b>I have to return to Zhcted for a while.</b>

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:08.980
<b>Huh?</b>

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.430
<b>A good friend of mine, a war maiden to whom I am indebted...</b>

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.050
<b>Her name's Alexandra Alshavin.</b>

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.130
<b>I call her Sasha.</b>

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.890
<b>She governs Regnitz.</b>

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:25.020
<b>And is under attack by another war maiden.</b>

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:28.040
<b>I have to defend her.</b>

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:28.890
<b>Defend her?</b>

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.890
<b>We promised each other!</b>

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.060
<b>Whenever one of us is in danger,</b>

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.070
<b>the other will come running, no matter what she is caught up in at the time.</b>

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.240
<b>You see, Sasha is terribly sick.</b>

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.450
<b>When I visited her this summer,</b>

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.200
<b>she was literally unable to walk on her own.</b>

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.540
<b>And yet Sasha's dragon gear still recognizes her as its owner.</b>

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:53.880
<b>That's why...</b>

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.520
<b>That's why I...</b>

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.000
<b>I get it.</b>

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:03.130
<b>I'll do my best while you're gone.</b>

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:08.680
<b>Thanks.</b>

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:15.650
<b>Roland stayed true to his word and set out alone.</b>

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.320
<b>Shortly thereafter he arrived in Nice.</b>

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.530
<b>I am Roland, of the Order of Navarre.</b>

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:24.280
<b>I must speak to His Royal Majesty about an urgent matter.</b>

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.410
<b>Please wait here.</b>

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.750
<b>Hey, Roland.</b>

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.130
<b>Ganelon?! What's going on here?!</b>

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.130
<b>You couldn't defeat the traitor,</b>

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.010
<b>yet you dare show your face in the capital?</b>

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:47.550
<b>I will be punishing your insolence in His Majesty's stead.</b>

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.560
<b>The venom of these bees can kill even a lion.</b>

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:56.520
<b>Enjoy being swarmed by thousands of them.</b>

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.570
<b>You're imprisoned with bees—an insectile hell.</b>

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:03.860
<b>Farewell, mightiest knight in all of Brune.</b>

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:06.780
<b>Roland...</b>

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.580
<b>Be a knight among knights.</b>

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.580
<b>Your Majesty...</b>

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.130
<b>We'll be back soon.</b>

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.720
<b>Sir Tigrevurmud, we'll meet again.</b>

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.890
<b>Thank you for your help. Take care.</b>

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.780
<b>Elen will be back right away.</b>

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.400
<b>Tough it out until then.</b>

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:46.030
<b>There's nothing greater for a man than to send a woman off with a smile, right?</b>

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.870
<b>Why'd you stay behind?</b>

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:55.000
<b>Winters here are a lot milder
compared to the ones at home.</b>

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:59.000
<b>And my new haircut made me a lot more sensitive to the cold.</b>

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.500
<b>I see.</b>

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:07.170
<b>A thousand Zhctedian soldiers stayed behind with me.</b>

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:11.760
<b>You've got our loyalty, Sir Tigrevurmud. Mine first and foremost.</b>

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.760
<b>I hope we'll be of use to you.</b>

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.390
<b>Roland is dead.</b>

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.150
<b>Word is that he was executed.</b>

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.520
<b>What's going on in that head of yours?!</b>

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.860
<b>Now what would this be about?</b>

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.570
<b>I mean Roland! Why'd you kill him?!</b>

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.780
<b>Oh...</b>

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:35.080
<b>Did you see him? He died standing up.</b>

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.540
<b>At least he was magnificent in death.</b>

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.830
<b>What about the western border?</b>

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.460
<b>Sachstein and Asvarre <i>will</i> take advantage of the situation!</b>

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:45.460
<b>What's done is done. Roland's dead.</b>

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.550
<b>Besides, our western borders are safe for now.</b>

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:51.470
<b>I'd be more worried about our southern neighbors.</b>

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:56.600
<b>A large army from Muozinel is advancing on us by land and sea.</b>

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.520
<b>I wonder how your people are doing...</b>

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.100
<b>Why, you...!</b>

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:12.160
<b>Of all the countries neighboring Brune, only Muozinel is practicing slavery.</b>

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:18.370
<b>Its forces would often invade other countries, slaughtering and plundering everything in their way.</b>

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:23.710
<b>There was no rhyme or reason to the raiders' targets, 
leaving the Kingdom of Brune at a loss.</b>

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.640
<b>Twenty thousand Muozinellan soldiers were currently attacking Brune.</b>

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.000
<b>In response, Thenardier split his forces in two.</b>

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.810
<b>He is heading south with a contingent of seven thousand soldiers.</b>

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:49.610
<b>Thenardier's plan calls for luring the Muozinellan army deeper into the country first,</b>

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:52.570
<b>leaving the borderlands undefended meanwhile.</b>

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:57.370
<b>Thenardier's remaining thirteen thousand men were sent to the capital under the pretext of protecting it.</b>

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:02.000
<b>In reality, they were to keep an eye on Ganelon,
who was mustering his army in the north.</b>

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:10.300
<b><i>Ganelon's under control for now, 
but what will the boy from Alsace do?</i></b>

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.600
<b><i>There's twenty thousand of them.</i></b>

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.850
<b><i>What to do?</i></b>

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:21.140
<b><i>Should I concentrate on bolstering our defense?</i></b>

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:22.770
<b><i>Then again...</i></b>

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.610
<b>I'll leave Durandal in your care.</b>

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:31.740
<b>It'll serve as proof that I, Roland, 
have recognized your cause as just.</b>

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.200
<b>My cause is just...</b>

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.660
<b>Lord Tigre, may I come in?</b>

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:40.040
<b>Is that you, Titta?</b>

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.000
<b>At this time of night?</b>

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.660
<b>It's morning already.</b>

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.420
<b>Let me guess: you stayed up all night?</b>

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:49.920
<b>Sorry.</b>

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.680
<b>Thanks. It was delicious.</b>

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.600
<b>Lord Tigre, you're the commanding officer.</b>

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.560
<b>You should make sure to get enough rest.</b>

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.980
<b>No need to worry.</b>

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.810
<b>Thanks to you, I've made up my mind.</b>

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:07.310
<b>Titta...</b>

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:09.440
<b>Yes?</b>

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.030
<b>We won't see each other for a while.</b>

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.820
<b>Please stay here with Bertrand.</b>

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:20.870
<b>Will you... come back to us safe and sound?</b>

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:21.910
<b>You have my word.</b>

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.830
<b>Can we win this?</b>

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:28.710
<b>I don't know.</b>

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.880
<b>You should at least say we've got a chance.</b>

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.220
<b>Else I won't be able to make the soldiers follow you.</b>

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:37.010
<b>They outnumber us twenty to one.</b>

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:39.850
<b>Who'd believe me if I claim we can pull this off?</b>

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.970
<b>People believe what they want to believe.</b>

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.570
<b>Please give us some hope.</b>

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:52.690
<b>I will head southeast together with a number of volunteers.</b>

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.860
<b>Our goals are to survive and to protect what must be protected.</b>

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:01.370
<b>If that's your goal, wouldn't it be better to bolster Territoire's defenses?</b>

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.700
<b>Even if we strengthen our defenses,</b>

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:07.250
<b>there's no guarantee we can hold out against that many enemies.</b>

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.550
<b>It would buy some time.</b>

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:12.840
<b>At least long enough for knights and soldiers from other noblemen to arrive.</b>

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:16.140
<b>We don't know if the enemy will even come to Territoire.</b>

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:18.630
<b>Or we could face the worst-case scenario.</b>

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:21.680
<b>You mean no one would come to our help?</b>

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.930
<b>Well, we are traitors to the throne.</b>

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:28.890
<b>There'd be no repercussions to anyone if we were left to die.</b>

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:32.270
<b>And that's why I need to ask you two for a favor.</b>

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.700
<b>It all started as a conflict between two noblemen.</b>

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:44.740
<b>Now Tigre leads seventeen hundred men in hope of preventing a national crisis.</b>

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.750
<b>Lord Tigre,</b>

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.750
<b>and everyone else...</b>

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:54.880
<b>Please, be safe.</b>

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.640
<b>Driving them out won't be enough.</b>

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.470
<b>I want to save as many people as we can.</b>

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.060
<b><i>I'll use this power.</i></b>

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.900
<b><i>No, I still haven't mastered it.</i></b>

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.480
<b><i>There's too many unknowns.</i></b>

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:19.120
<b>Shall we take aim?</b>

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.280
<b>That's for tomorrow.</b>

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.110
<b>Today we're scouting to prepare.</b>

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.200
<b>Yes, of course.</b>

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:30.500
<b>By the way, what do you make of Viscount Augre's son?</b>

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:31.870
<b>Gerald?</b>

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:35.170
<b>He's good with numbers and accurate in his work.</b>

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:39.010
<b>It's thanks to him that I could focus on fighting during the battle with Roland.</b>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:44.180
<b>Hm, there's something off about him.</b>

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.640
<b>It feels like he's always looking down on others.</b>

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:49.900
<b>Hey now, let's all get along.</b>

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:50.770
<b>Footsteps?</b>

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:12.920
<b>Are you all right?</b>

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:21.720
<b>You don't need to be afraid.</b>

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.050
<b>I'm Tigrevurmud Vorn.</b>

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:24.970
<b>I'm a Bruneman.</b>

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.650
<b>Tigre... vurmud.</b>

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.070
<b>Hey, Rurick!</b>

